+# Agent Note: model-input host provenance
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-29-model-input-host-provenance.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Host policy needs to identify which configured plugin contributed each model-visible prompt section, runtime context, and tool schema before deciding what an assembly may retain. Contribution names are model-facing registry keys, not owner identities, and Cordis plugin display names are optional and non-unique. Adding provenance as assembly fields would also expose host policy metadata to LLM requests and JSON transports.
+
+## Decision
+
+`dsh-system-prompt` captures a branded `HostSourceId` when each section, context, or schema provider registers. It walks the actual calling Cordis fiber to its owning Loader Entry and combines the entry's full configured path with a stable tree namespace. A file-backed tree derives an opaque namespace from its resolved configuration filename, so a standing preset keeps its sources across process and fiber replacement while two preset files may reuse row ids without collision. Root Loader entries use their root namespace. A registration outside Loader composition receives the single recognizable `UNKNOWN_HOST_SOURCE_ID`; display names and callback names never substitute for configured identity, and source ids do not expose filenames.
+
+The registry stores source beside its registration. Scoped merging therefore selects the source and contribution together, including same-name shadows. `dsh-tools` applies the same rule to each tool definition and returns per-schema source ids through its dynamic prompt provider, so one provider invocation can project tools from different owners without collapsing their provenance to the tools service.
+
+Assembly entry objects are keys in a private `WeakMap`. `promptAssemblySourceInventory()` derives a current ordered inventory from those identities. Object-spreading an assembly retains the entry identities and their provenance; a listener that creates or copies an entry receives the explicit unknown source. No source is an enumerable assembly, section, context, or tool field, so normal request construction and JSON serialization cannot transmit it.
+
+`SystemPrompt.admitSources()` registers synchronous predicates in the same global or scoped layers as prompt contributions. Every effective predicate observes every effective registry candidate and all must accept it. Sections are admitted before complete-section selection and text evaluation, contexts before text evaluation, and dynamic tool results schema by schema using each schema's effective source. A rejected complete section cannot be restored after the waterfall. The waterfall remains responsible for entries its listeners create because those entries do not come from the registry.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Host policy can admit registry contributions by unambiguous live configured-plugin ownership without importing Loader, inspecting Cordis internals, or mutating wire objects.
+- A source id remains a persistent policy key while its file-backed tree keeps the same resolved filename and configured entry ids. Changing either intentionally creates a new source.
+- Direct programmatic plugins remain observable as unknown. A future host that needs out-of-Loader identity must add a separate explicit registration identity rather than infer a display or callback name.
+- Provenance follows retained entry identity through a waterfall. Reconstructed entries deliberately lose attribution instead of inheriting it by matching names.
+- Admission predicates compose conjunctively across global and inherited scoped layers, retain independent effect lifetimes, and still observe candidates that another predicate rejects so inventory collection is complete.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **Use contribution names or Cordis `fiber.name` / `runtime.name`** — rejected because these values describe presentation or registry slots, can repeat, and do not identify the configured owner.
+- **Use bare Loader `entry.id` or Cordis fiber uid** — rejected because bare entry ids can repeat across standing preset files, while fiber uid changes across reload and is cleared on disposal.
+- **Add source fields to `PromptAssembly` and `ToolSchema`** — rejected because ordinary spread and JSON transport would make host policy metadata model-visible and wire-visible.
+- **Require every registrar to pass a source id** — rejected for Loader composition because its stable tree namespace and configured entry path are automatic. Explicit ids remain the correct extension for provenance outside Loader.
+- **Filter only in `system-prompt/assemble` waterfall listeners** — rejected because complete-section restoration can override listener filtering and registry providers would already have been evaluated. Listener-created entries remain outside registry admission by design.
